---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const updated = 'July 18, 2026';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of Service | nPower Software"
  description="Terms governing use of the nPower Software and Power Surfacing website operated by IntegrityWare, Inc."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <article class="bg-white py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-red-600 mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 mb-3">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-10">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="legal-copy space-y-9 text-slate-700 leading-7">
        <section>
          <h2>Agreement to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service govern your use of the nPower Software and Power Surfacing
            website operated by IntegrityWare, Inc. By accessing or using this website, you agree
            to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the website.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Website information</h2>
          <p>
            The website provides information about our software, pricing, trials, workflows,
            tutorials, support resources, events, and resellers. We may update, correct, suspend,
            or remove website content at any time. Product availability, features, compatibility,
            pricing, and promotions may change and should be confirmed before purchase.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Software licenses and purchases</h2>
          <p>
            These website terms do not grant a license to any software. Downloads, trials,
            subscriptions, maintenance, and purchased software are governed by the applicable
            end-user license agreement, quote, order, invoice, or other written agreement. If
            those terms conflict with these website terms regarding software or a purchase, the
            applicable software or transaction agreement controls.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>You agree not to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>use the website in violation of applicable law or another person’s rights;</li>
            <li>attempt to gain unauthorized access to the website or related systems;</li>
            <li>interfere with website security, availability, or operation;</li>
            <li>introduce malicious code or use automated means that impose an unreasonable load; or</li>
            <li>misrepresent your identity or submit fraudulent or misleading information.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The website and its text, graphics, logos, videos, software descriptions, and other
            content are owned by IntegrityWare, Inc. or its licensors and are protected by
            intellectual-property laws. You may view and print reasonable portions for your own
            lawful business evaluation or personal use. No other rights are granted without our
            written permission. Third-party names and trademarks belong to their respective owners.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>User communications</h2>
          <p>
            You are responsible for information you submit through the website. You represent that
            you have the right to provide it and that it does not violate law or another person’s
            rights. Do not submit confidential design files, regulated data, or sensitive personal
            information unless we have agreed in writing to receive it through an appropriate channel.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
          <p>
            The website may link to resellers, videos, maps, social platforms, or other third-party
            services. We do not control those services and are not responsible for their content,
            availability, security, or privacy practices. A link does not necessarily imply endorsement.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by law, the website and its content are provided “as is”
            and “as available.” We disclaim warranties regarding accuracy, completeness, availability,
            non-infringement, merchantability, and fitness for a particular purpose. Nothing on this
            website constitutes engineering, manufacturing, legal, or other professional advice.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by law, IntegrityWare, Inc. and its officers, employees,
            and affiliates will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
            punitive damages arising from use of, or inability to use, this website. Rights that cannot
            lawfully be excluded or limited remain unaffected.
