          <h2>Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to its
            conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute concerning these website terms will be brought in the
            state or federal courts located in San Diego County, California, unless applicable law
            requires otherwise.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms by posting a revised version on this page. The “Last updated”
            date above identifies the current version. Continued use after an update constitutes
            acceptance of the revised terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms may be sent to{' '}
            <a href="mailto:info@npowersoftware.com">info@npowersoftware.com</a> or IntegrityWare,
            Inc., P.O. Box 722962, San Diego, CA 92172-2962, United States.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .legal-copy h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; color: rgb(15 23 42); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .legal-copy p + p { margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .legal-copy ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin: 0.75rem 0; }
  .legal-copy li + li { margin-top: 0.35rem; }
  .legal-copy a { color: rgb(220 38 38); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
